<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n41735" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">rĭcĭnus</span></b> ,
			i, m.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A large kind of vermin that infests sheep</i>, <i>dogs</i>, etc., <i>a tick</i>, <i>tike</i>, <i><span class="en">Cato, R. R. 96,
			2</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Varr. R. R. 2, 9, 14</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Col. 7, 13,
				1</span></i>; <i><span class="en">6, 2,
			6</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 22, 18, 21, § 47</span></i>;
					<i><span class="en">Petr. 57</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Ser.
					Samm. 36, 699</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A plant</i>, <i>called also</i> cici
				<i>and</i> croton, <i><span class="en">Plin. 15, 7,
				7, § 25</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>III.</b>
			<i>The germ of the mulberry</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ricino Graeci vocant,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					23, 7, 71, § 137</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
